course: dictionary
lesson: 11825
title: Bisect: cutting in two
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To bisect something means to cut it into two parts. In maths, you bisect a line when you cut it into two equal parts, so each half is the same length. «Use your ruler to bisect the line at its middle point.» The word bisect is built from bi, which means two, and sect, which means cut.
explain: Bisect does not always mean equal parts. «The river bisects the town, so one side is north and one side is south.» The river cuts across the town, but the two sides may be very different sizes. Ask yourself: does the text say the parts are equal? If not, the parts may be unequal.
explain: In geometry, you can bisect an angle too. «The angle bisector cuts the angle into two equal angles.» A compass and a ruler help you do this neatly. Check the meaning by swapping in "cut into two" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Bisect is a verb. Its other forms are bisects, bisected and bisecting.
fact: «Bisect» means to cut or divide something into two equal parts, in maths.
fact: «Bisect» can also mean to cut across something and divide it into two parts that are not always equal.
fact: A perpendicular bisector cuts a line in half at a right angle, which is a corner of 90 degrees.
fact: Bi means two, so bisect means cut in two. Other words with bi: bicycle, bilingual.
exercise: «Use your ruler and compass to bisect the line.» What does bisect mean here? | Measure its length in centimetres | Colour it in | Join two lines together | *Cut into two equal parts
exercise: «The river bisects the town.» What does bisect mean in this sentence? | Makes the town smaller | *Cuts across the town, dividing it into two parts | Fills the town with water | Moves the town to another place
exercise: Tom says bisect means to join two things together. Is he right? | Yes, it means to join | Yes, it means to measure | *No, it means to cut something into two parts | No, it means to paint something
test: An angle bisector cuts an angle into two equal angles. What does it do to the angle? | Turns it into a straight line | *Splits it into two equal parts | Measures its size | Makes it bigger
test: «The road bisects the park.» Are the two parts of the park always the same size? | There are no parts at all | *No, not always equal | Yes, always exactly equal | Yes, because bisect means equal
exam: «A perpendicular bisector does what to a line?» | *Cuts it in half at a right angle | Draws it in red | Joins it to another line | Makes the line longer
